       These functions return a representation (determined by _t_a_g_p) of a quiet
       NaN.   If  the  implementation does not support quiet NaNs, these func‐
       tions return zero.

       The call _n_a_n_(_"_c_h_a_r_-_s_e_q_u_e_n_c_e_"_) is equivalent to:

           strtod("NAN(char-sequence)", NULL);

       Similarly, calls to nnaannff() and nnaannll() are equivalent to analogous calls
       to ssttrrttooff(3) and ssttrrttoolldd(3).

       The argument _t_a_g_p is used in an unspecified manner.  On IEEE  754  sys‐
       tems,  there are many representations of NaN, and _t_a_g_p selects one.  On
       other systems it may do nothing.

